---

## alwaysApply: true

# CORE PRINCIPLES

* Explicit > clever
* 1 function = 1 responsibility
* No dead code / TODO

# ARCHITECTURE (MANDATORY)

* Laravel:

  * Controller must be thin
  * Business logic → Service
* Vue:

  * No API calls in component
  * Component → Store → Service

# SCOPE CONTROL (CRITICAL)

* Only modify what is explicitly requested
* Do NOT refactor unrelated code
* Do NOT change architecture unless asked
* Prefer minimal changes over large rewrites

# CODE QUALITY

* Clean, readable, maintainable
* Avoid over-engineering
* Prefer simple and correct solution

# UI/UX STANDARD

* Clean, minimal, no visual noise
* No tooltip / helper text unless required
* Consistent spacing and layout
* Use Tailwind (utility-first)

# INTERACTION RULES

* Show loading state when needed
* Disable actions while processing
* Confirm destructive actions (delete, etc.)
* Provide success / error feedback

# PERFORMANCE AWARENESS

* Avoid unnecessary re-render (Vue)
* Avoid N+1 queries (Laravel)
* Do not introduce heavy logic in UI layer

# RESPONSE RULES

* Return only necessary code
* Do not include unrelated changes
* Explain briefly in Vietnamese if needed

# SAFETY RULES

* Do not break existing behavior
* No side effects
* No hidden logic changes

# DEFAULT MINDSET

* Think before coding
* Fix root cause, not symptoms
* Optimize for long-term maintainability
